Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:50:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: Add the Apple S8000 USB role switch

The Apple A9 (S8000/S8003) USB complex has a device-only DWC2 and a
separate EHCI + OHCI host pair behind one AUSB PHY. A USB_CTL register
bank selects whether the PHY serves the host pair. On the iPad 5 the
Lightning port reaches the host pair only through this switch.

Describe the switch: its USB_CTL bank, the shared PHY, the DWC2 whose
gadget it disconnects in the host role, and the EHCI and OHCI child
nodes, which the switch creates only in the host role. A Lightning board
also names the PMIC with the accessory power LDO and the Tristar port
controller, whose ACC pin routing is set up before accessory power is
turned on.

Assisted-by: LLM
